---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Tenancy Agreement Review Ghana — Act 220 Compliance Check | PRC" description="Get your lease, offer letter, or notice reviewed for Act 220 compliance. Catch gaps before they become disputes.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/services/" style="color:#516784; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1rem; display:inline-block;">← Back to Services</a>

      <h1>Tenancy Documentation Review</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px; margin-bottom:2rem;">Get your lease, offer letter, tenancy notice, or other agreement reviewed line-by-line against Ghana's Act 220 requirements. Spot gaps and compliance issues before they become disputes.</p>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f0f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Why You Need This Service</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;">A badly written or incomplete tenancy document is one of the biggest causes of rent disputes in Ghana. Here's what can go wrong:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8; margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <li><strong>Missing mandatory clauses:</strong> Act 220 requires specific language on termination, rent, and dispute procedures</li>
          <li><strong>Unclear terms:</strong> Vague language leads to misunderstandings and arguments</li>
          <li><strong>Illegal clauses:</strong> Some practices landlords think are legal actually violate Act 220</li>
          <li><strong>Unenforceable provisions:</strong> A poorly drafted clause might not hold up in Rent Court</li>
          <li><strong>Missing evidence:</strong> When disputes arise, weak documentation means weak position</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;"><strong>This service ensures your documents are legally sound and defensible.</strong> We review whatever you have and mark it up with corrections, gaps, and explanations.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What We Review</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Lease agreements (residential, commercial, furnished, month-to-month)</li>
          <li>Tenancy offer letters</li>
          <li>Renewal agreements</li>
          <li>Termination notices</li>
          <li>Rent increase notices</li>
          <li>Any other tenancy-related document</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What You Get</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Marked-Up Document:</strong> Your document with corrections, suggestions, and explanations</li>
          <li><strong>Compliance Summary:</strong> Which Act 220 requirements are met and which are missing</li>
          <li><strong>Risk Assessment:</strong> Clauses that might not hold up in Rent Court</li>
          <li><strong>Recommendations:</strong> What to change or add before using with tenant</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#fff3cd; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">When You Need This Service</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li>You have a template lease and want to check if it's compliant</li>
          <li>You've drafted your own agreement and want a professional review</li>
          <li>A tenant has disputed terms and you want to know your position</li>
          <li>You're using an old lease from years ago and aren't sure if it's still valid</li>
          <li>You want to make sure all your documents use consistent, legal language</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#e8f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Common Issues We Catch</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Missing rent payment date and method</li>
          <li>No termination clause or incorrect notice period</li>
          <li>Illegal penalty clauses or forfeiture language</li>
          <li>Unclear maintenance and repair responsibilities</li>
          <li>Missing tenant rights and dispute procedures</li>
          <li>Inconsistent dates or incomplete descriptions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Pricing & Turnaround</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.2rem; font-weight:700; color:#516784; margin:0;">GHS 150 per agreement</p>
        <p style="color:#666; margin:0.5rem 0;">One fixed price regardless of length or complexity</p>
        <p style="font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem;">Turnaround: 1–2 working days</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:3rem 0; text-align:center;">
        <a href="/services/" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#516784; color:white; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; margin-right:1rem;">Request a Quote</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/233208071633" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#f0f4f8; color:#516784; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; border:1px solid #516784;">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
